{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>I</b> — Know that the wife of Jacob our father is Rachel, and Leah was concealed in her place. Also Rachel gave her handmaid to him, and on account of Leah's jealousy, the other handmaid was also given to him. Therefore when Rachel bore Joseph she said, Send me, and Jacob said to Ephraim and Manasseh, <i>and let my name be called upon them</i> (Genesis 48:16). Therefore all Israel is called Ephraim. And Yefet said: Perhaps the kingdom of Jehu was from Ephraim, and because he found Ramoth-Gilead to be Gadite, he needed to say it is not the one written in the words of Jehu, and in the book of Amos I will explain that he is from Ephraim. And the correct view in my eyes: that when our fathers came to the land of Canaan, Judah stood on his border to the south and the house of Joseph, which is all the tribe of Ephraim and half the tribe of Manasseh, to the north; therefore Judah and Ephraim are mentioned, and so in Jeremiah: <i>Is Ephraim a dear son to Me</i> (Jeremiah 31:19), and there was no king in those days from Ephraim." "<b>You have played the harlot</b> — Your soul also after others."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:17.211949749Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}